Dear Vincent,

I hope this message finds you well. I recently upgraded GGIR from version 3.0.1 to 3.0.2 and successfully generated part 2 output data. However, I encountered two warning messages during this process:

Warning messages:
1: In filesummary[vi:(vi + 6)] <- c(file_summary$Dur_imputed, file_summary$Dur_chsum_failed, :
number of items to replace is not a multiple of replacement length
2: In filesummary[vi:(vi + 6)] <- c(file_summary$Nblocks_imputed, file_summary$Nblocks_chsum_failed, :
number of items to replace is not a multiple of replacement length

I am seeking clarification on how these warnings are generated and whether it is advisable to ignore them.

Additionally, I am curious about the compatibility of milestone data generated by the older version GGIR 3.0.1. If I set overwrite=F, can all milestone data from part 1 be safely reused with the new version?

Your insights and suggestions on these matters would be greatly appreciated.

Best regards,
Margaret

