Dear Vincent,

I have some new findings. While investigating milestone data in part 1 from GGIR version 3.0.1, I noticed a notable difference. The CWA file, previously flagged as corrupt and too short (3.0.1: "M$filecorrupt=True", "M$filetooshort=True"), is now recognized as normal in version 3.0.2 with both parameters set to False.

I am eager to understand the reasons behind this change. Could you provide insights into why the recognition status of this CWA file has shifted between the two versions?

Your guidance on this matter would be highly appreciated.

Best regards, Margaret.

