Hi Jane

My approach when working with the 2011-2014 NHANES data was to first merge all .csv files per participant (parallelised on a cluster) and then continue processing the combined .csv files with GGIR. Haven’t tried the function Jairo suggested yet but depending on the package you’re using, combining .csv files before using GGIR might be faster.

Cheers

Fabian

